  "description": "1. User requested that the Chat component's file list adopt the `ChatEntry` chip-style design, calling out the hover-reveal of actions as poor design\u2014especially on mobile.\n\n2. I identified the root problems in `ChatFileList.vue`: actions hidden behind `hidden md:flex group-hover:flex`, making them unreachable on touch devices and pointer-dependent on desktop.\n\n3. I proposed reworking the file list into compact `ChatEntry`-style chips (`rounded-md`, `bg-base-200` / `bg-primary/10`) with the label as a real `<button>` and actions rendered always-visible.\n\n4. Two files were modified: `ChatFileList.vue` (template chips, header, empty state) and `FileActionMenu.vue` (tighter `gap-0.5`, `p-1` tap targets, `hover:bg-base-content/10`, added `aria-label`s).\n\n5. All existing props, emits, watchers, and methods were preserved, so no changes to `Chat.vue` were required\u2014delivering a touch-friendly, accessible, WCAG-compliant file list.",
